✅ Final Smart Wheelchair Project Parts List
1️⃣ Main Controller & Vision

Raspberry Pi 4 Model B (4 GB RAM)

Pi Camera Module V2 (8 MP)

MicroSD Card 32 GB Class 10

SD Card Reader (USB)

Heatsink + Fan kit for Pi (optional)

2️⃣ Wireless Control Modules

ESP32 Dev Board WROOM‑32 ×2 (one for glove, one for wheelchair receiver)

3️⃣ GSM / GPS / Alerts

SIM800L V2 GSM Module with antenna

NEO‑6M GPS Module

DS3231 RTC Module

Active Buzzer 5 V

4️⃣ Audio / Voice Interaction

INMP441 I²S Microphone Module

USB-powered speaker (instead of PAM8403 amp + passive speaker)

5️⃣ Motors / Movement / Sensors

BTS7960 Dual H‑Bridge Motor Driver Module ×2

12 V 300 RPM Geared DC Motors ×4

MPU6050 Gyro + Accelerometer Module

HC‑SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor (optional)

Tactile Push Buttons ×3

1‑Channel 5 V Relay Module (optional)

6️⃣ Power & Wiring – Wheelchair Side

12 V 3S Li‑Ion 18650 Battery Pack with BMS

Buck Converter #1: 12 V → 5.1 V, ≥5 A output (Pi + peripherals)

Buck Converter #2: 12 V → 4.0 V, ≥3 A output (SIM800L)

Electrolytic Capacitors: 2200–4700 µF, low ESR ×2

Ceramic Capacitors: 0.1 µF ×2

XT60 Connectors (male + female)

Silicone Wires 14–16 AWG (1 m pair)

Inline Fuse (rated for motor current)

KCD4 Rocker Switch (main power ON/OFF)

Terminal Blocks ×4–6

7️⃣ Power & Wiring – Glove Side

5 V USB Power Bank, 5000 mAh, ≥2 A output

USB Cable to ESP32

Optional: 470 µF Electrolytic + 0.1 µF Ceramic Capacitor across VIN/GND of ESP32 for extra stability

8️⃣ Misc / Accessories

Jumper Wires (Dupont)

Heat-Shrink Tubing

Velcro / Double-Sided Tape

Plastic Project Boxes / Enclosures

Digital Multimeter (DT830D or UNI-T UT33C+)

Extra wires, zip-ties, cable management
